    | Jan Klimke, member of the HPI Computer Graphics Systems group and member of the HPI Research School on Service-oriented Computing, gave a talk on “Service-based interactive 3D Visualization of massive 3D City Models on Thin Clients” at the Plenary Session of the 
    a.external-link-new-window(href="http://www.sig3d.de/" target="_blank" title="Öffnet externen Link in neuem Fenster") Special Interest Group 3D (SIG3D)
    | , which was held at the Hamburg Surveying and Geoinformation Agency on October 14th, 2011.
